oke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"432\" y1=\"23\" x2=\"440\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"444\" y1=\"23\" x2=\"452\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"456\" y1=\"23\" x2=\"464\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"468\" y1=\"23\" x2=\"476\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"480\" y1=\"23\" x2=\"488\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"492\" y1=\"23\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"504\" y1=\"23\" x2=\"512\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"516\" y1=\"23\" x2=\"524\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"24\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"64\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#B9C2C7\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"64\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#1F2A28\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"174\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"204\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"174\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"184\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"184\" width=\"40\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#B9C2C7\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"194.7\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"194.7\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"205.3\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"205.3\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1F2A28\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">m</text><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"214\" width=\"40\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#B9C2C7\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"224.7\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"224.7\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"235.3\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"235.3\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"235\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1F2A28\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2m</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F2A28\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Setup A</text><line x1=\"390\" y1=\"24\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"390\" cy=\"64\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#B9C2C7\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"390\" cy=\"64\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#1F2A28\"/><line x1=\"370\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"174\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><line x1=\"410\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"204\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><line x1=\"370\" y1=\"174\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"184\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"350\" y=\"184\" width=\"40\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#B9C2C7\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"350\" y1=\"194.7\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"194.7\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"350\" y1=\"205.3\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"205.3\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1F2A28\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2m</text><line x1=\"410\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"390\" y=\"214\" width=\"40\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#B9C2C7\" stroke=\"#1F2A28\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"390\" y1=\"224.7\" x2=\"430\" y2=\"224.7\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"390\" y1=\"235.3\" x2=\"430\" y2=\"235.3\" stroke=\"#5A6268\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"410\" y=\"235\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1F2A28\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3m</text><text x=\"390\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F2A28\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Setup B</text></svg></div>"},"parts":[{"label":"a","prompt":"In which setup is the size of the blocks' acceleration greater? <b>Justify</b> your claim qualitatively, with no equations or calculations.","points":3,"rubric":[{"point":"Claims setup A has the greater acceleration","accept":["A accelerates faster"]},{"point":"The unbalanced pull (difference in weights) is the same in both: one block heavier by m, so the same net force on each system","accept":["both have a net force equal to the weight of a mass m"]},{"point":"Setup B has more total mass to accelerate (5m vs 3m), so the same net force gives it a smaller acceleration","accept":["more inertia in B, same net force"]}],"sample":"Setup A. In both setups the heavier side outweighs the lighter side by the weight of a mass m, so the net external force that drives each system along the string is the same. But setup B has to accelerate more mass in all, 5m instead of 3m, so the same net force gives it a smaller acceleration."},{"label":"b","prompt":"For an Atwood machine with blocks of mass m₁ and m₂ (m₂ > m₁), <b>derive</b> an expression for the size of the acceleration in terms of m₁, m₂ and physical constants. Begin your derivation with Newton's second law.","points":3,"rubric":[{"point":"Applies Newton's second law to the system (or to each block)","accept":["ΣF = m_sys a","two equations: F_T − m₁g = m₁a and m₂g − F_T = m₂a"]},{"point":"Net force along the string is m₂g − m₁g, with tension internal (or eliminated)","accept":["tension cancels when the two equations are added"]},{"point":"a = (m₂ − m₁)g / (m₁ + m₂)","accept":["a = g(m₂ − m₁)/(m₂ + m₁)"]}],"sample":"Take the two blocks and the string as the system, positive in the direction m₂ moves (down on its side, up on the other). The tension is internal. Newton's second law: ΣF = m_sys a, with ΣF = m₂g − m₁g and m_sys = m₁ + m₂. So a = (m₂ − m₁)g / (m₁ + m₂)."},{"label":"c","prompt":"Use your expression from part (b) to <b>explain</b> whether it supports your claim in part (a).","points":2,"rubric":[{"point":"Substitutes: setup A gives a = (2m − m)g/(3m) = g/3; setup B gives a = (3m − 2m)g/(5m) = g/5","accept":["g/3 and g/5"]},{"point":"Concludes that g/3 > g/5, which supports the claim that A accelerates more, tying it to the same numerator and larger denominator","accept":["same top (mg), bigger bottom in B, so the expression agrees with part (a)"]}],"sample":"Setup A: a = (2m − m)g/(m + 2m) = g/3. Setup B: a = (3m − 2m)g/(2m + 3m) = g/5. The numerators are the same (the same net force, mg), and B's denominator is larger (more mass), so A's acceleration g/3 is larger than B's g/5. This supports my claim."}]}